A crude diagram on lined paper.
 Reading left-to-right,
 we put the number one on a stack,
 followed by 2 on top of it.
 The (+) function then takes two values off the stack,
 and puts down a 3 instead.
 After 4 is pushed to that stack on top of the 3,
 (*) takes both to produce the final result on the stack,
 12.
