\begin_layout Section*
A quick-ish recap
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We’ve already done a lot.
 A remarkable amount.
 So far we’ve discovered that everyone believes their particular baroque,
 archaic and inconsistent number system is not just pretty,
 but pretty damn near perfect.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "Whether you have"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/counting-from-zero"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 a body part tally system,
 a decimal system,
 or the numerical word web of the Nasioi that counts houses or tens of opossums with one convention,
 and dance troupes (or bundles of bamboo) with another.
 Let’s not even talk about 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "the English"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/sing-a-song-of-sixpence"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 who stole eleven (ęndleofan) from I know not where,
 and seem to have slotted in an Arabic/Indian counting system more-or-less back-to-front.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This problem is even worse in Computer Science,
 where we are all absolutely certain that alone among the hundreds of languages our one is The Way,
 whether we 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "count up from (or down to) one or zero"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/210541344/counter-intuitive"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 and regardless of pretty much everything else we do.
 To our consternation,
 we discovered that in 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "floating point arithmetic"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/212226868/but"
literal "false"

\end_inset

:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
But more than this,
 we bumped into the perils of cut-and-paste,
 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "the meaning of foo"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/the-summoning-of-spirits"
literal "false"

\end_inset

—
it’s a verb :) We found value in being able to identify 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "at a glance"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/212130688/lets-start-building"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 what something does.
 In 
\series bold
\emph on
Zyzyxia
\series default
\emph default
,
 form follows function:
 from a mile away,
 we can spot a verb,
 a Noun,
 an ugly shouty COMMAND,
 an _adverb_ and even a nasty little camelCase parochialValue,
 which some might know as “a local variable”.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "Then"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/223706357/complexity-is-easy"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 we even discovered parochial-like atoms:
 rE and xE,
 which are convenient “trumps”—
fake parochials.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "Polish notation"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/lets-polish-our-polish"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 next sucked us in,
 as with it we can utterly discard the seventeen layers of operator precedence in languages like C++.
 We found that 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "FORTH allows us to discard in turn"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/213376055/going-forth-using-reverse-polish"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 all of the irritating parentheses of Lisp—
it uses Reverse Polish Notation.
 We found the 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "joy of recursion"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/213376055/a-very-cool-thing"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
And then we met 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "POWER notation"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/213376055/power"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 which reverses FORTH and writes Polish,
 but evaluates from right-to-left.
 It reads well,
 and works without parentheses or precedence rules.
 We saw how powerful (pun intended) it is to use a stack.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We also stole—
from the J language—
the idea of manipulating a whole list in one action.
 Continuing this same happy thread,
 we 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "bumped into The Enemy once more"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/214247059/claude-codea-case-study"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
 Complexity.
 Here personified in Claude Code,
