\begin_layout Standard
\SpecialChar ldots
 and this in turn gave us the Write Once Read Many principle (WORM).
 As a side effect,
 Global values lost all of their terror (almost),
 and we saw how immutably writing the value of a variable encourages us to 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "write simpler code"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/219692586/3-local-variables"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Some 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "expensive explosions"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/the-wrath-of-kahan"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 showed the merit of strong typing.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "Fibonacci numbers"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/220506032/aww-lets-play-with-phyllotaxis"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 convinced us that the wrong algorithm will bring the most powerful supercomputer to its knees.
 We also saw how fixed-point inaccuracies allowed hackers to steak $128 million from Balancer in just 30 minutes,
 and how some algorithms are just intrinsically nasty,
 disabling even extremely precise calculations.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
After touching on 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "modules"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/221890680/modules"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 we glanced at 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "Zipf’s law"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/220506032/aww-lets-play-with-phyllotaxis"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 and stole its main theme as the principle:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\emph on
Keep your names long.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We then 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "built the core"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/a-language-in-7-lines"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 of 
\series bold
\emph on
Zyzyxia
\series default
\emph default
 in just 7 lines,
 which led to simple 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "flow of control"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/almost-in-circles"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 —
and then most of my readers rather lost it.
 My apologies!
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
But the ideas are simple.
 There are alternatives to hoppin’ in the middle like a herring on the griddle.
 And if you simply must jump around,
 do so in an orderly manner using simple constructs like { | } CASE and { } REPEAT.
 Enough said.
\end_layout

